      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-287091",
      ":question/problem": "A film director is hiring $x$ camera operators and $y$ sound engineers for a movie project. The director must hire at least $18$ people in total, but wants to keep the total weekly pay at no more than $$14, 000$. If each camera operator will be paid $$800$ per week and each sound engineer will be paid $$1, 000$ per week, and the director must hire at least $6$ camera operators and at least $3$ sound engineers, which of the following systems of inequalities represents this situation?"
