      ":question/problem": "A farmer is purchasing $x$ bags of grain and $y$ water tanks for livestock. The farmer must purchase at least $25$ items in total, but wants to spend no more than $$7, 000$. If each bag of grain costs $$120$ and each water tank costs $$350$, and the farmer must buy at least $10$ bags of grain and at least $5$ water tanks, which of the following systems of inequalities represents this situation?"
